# HireSphere tech stack (locked)

Canonical source: `openspec/project.md`. **Do not deviate** unless the user explicitly approves a stack change in writing.

## Allowed stack

| Layer | Use | Do not use |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend | React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS v4 | Next.js, Angular, Vue, plain CSS frameworks outside Tailwind v4 |
| API | Node.js, **Fastify**, REST `/api/v1` | Express, Python/FastAPI, Django, Go, serverless frameworks outside Cloud Run |
| Workers | Cloud Run + **Pub/Sub** | SQS, RabbitMQ, Celery, cron-only without Pub/Sub |
| Database | **Cloud SQL PostgreSQL 15**, **Drizzle ORM** | MySQL, MongoDB, Prisma, TypeORM, Supabase as primary DB |
| Storage | **GCS**, signed URLs | S3, local disk in prod, public buckets |
| AI | **Vertex AI (Gemini)** via `packages/ai-prompts` | OpenAI direct, Anthropic direct, unversioned inline prompts |
| OCR | **Document AI** | Tesseract-only for production path |
| Auth | **JWT** (access + refresh), **bcrypt** | Hubble SSO, OAuth/SSO, session cookies without spec approval |
| IaC | **Terraform** in `infra/terraform/` | Pulumi, CDK, click-ops-only infra |
| CI/CD | **Cloud Build** | GitHub Actions as primary deploy (unless user adds later) |
| Monorepo | **pnpm** workspaces: `apps/web`, `apps/api`, `services/worker`, `packages/*` | npm/yarn without approval, single-package repo layout |

## Architecture rules

- Business logic lives in API/worker — **not** in React beyond presentation.
- Use platform adapters in `packages/shared` (`StorageProvider`, `JobQueue`, `AIProvider`).
- RBAC on every protected endpoint; never trust UI-only hiding.
- Migrations are additive only — never edit shipped migration files.

## Scope exclusions (never add without explicit approval)

- Hubble SSO / Hubble login
- Miracle branding or assets
- Feature flags product (v1 uses RBAC permissions instead)

## Before proposing alternatives

Ask: *"Does this need a stack change, or can the approved stack do it?"* Default answer: use the approved stack.
